1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:05,890
Make common denominators of two fractions.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:34,520
Example 4: Given two fractions one-half and one-third, find two fractions with same denominator, among them one fraction equals one-half and one fraction equals one-third.

3
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:44,560
Essentially we make common denominators of two fractions one-half and one-third.

4
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:56,970
To make common denominators of two fractions one-half and one-third, we do how many steps, which steps?

5
00:01:06,050 --> 00:01:10,750
Multiply both numerator and denominator of one-half by three

6
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:22,000
Multiply both numerator and denominator of one-third by two.

7
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:37,760
We say two fractions one-half and one-third have been made common denominators into two fractions three-sixths and two-sixths.

8
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:49,730
Six is called common denominator of two fractions three-sixths and two-sixths.

9
00:01:54,100 --> 00:02:03,340
Common denominator divides evenly by denominator of two fractions one-half and one-third.

10
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:12,280
Conclusion: To make common denominators of two fractions we do as follows.

11
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:24,620
Take numerator and denominator of first fraction multiply by denominator of second fraction.

12
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:35,980
Take numerator and denominator of second fraction multiply by denominator of first fraction.

